--
N5008 [meta.trans.other] decay: libstdc++ 16 implements std::decay with
GCC's __decay(T) builtin.  The front end parses __decay as __remove_cvref
(parse.cpp), so an array or function type does not decay to a pointer
(std::__decay_t<int[5]> is int[5]); a function type written without a
reference, `__decay(int(long))', is also a parse error.  Found while
reducing the libstdc++ 16 ranges failure (iterator_t of an array inside
ranges::__access::__member_begin); not the root cause of a CORE failure.
g++ 16 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion (g++ 13 has no __decay).
